  "caveats": [
    "Very few in-universe events: holdout positives are a few dozen package-window hits (see *_holdout_positive_labels). Events cluster in campaigns, so the effective sample is smaller still. Significance is weak; treat CIs as rough.",
    "Most MAL events are out-of-universe: the package's first advisory lands inside the window. Neither model can price those, so the reported base rates describe only packages already listed in OSV before the anchor.",
    "Universe = packages named in any OSV advisory in the bulk zip. npm GHSA entries are a small share, so the universe is mostly MAL-listed packages; it is not the registry.",
    "The OSV zip is a 2026-10 snapshot. Published dates are used, but withdrawals and re-listings after each anchor are not reconstructed.",
    "Alpha is chosen on tune-period (pre-2024) log loss and then scored on holdout. Holdout is still one period; the choice is not re-validated across regimes.",
    "The const model is an expanding-window monthly hazard per ecosystem, not a fixed constant; it is a baseline, not a market price.",
    "Bootstrap resamples evaluation months (anchors) and ignores within-month correlation between packages, so intervals are optimistic if campaigns cluster across packages."
  ]
